    "title": "Where to stream Ryan Gosling's ‘Project Hail Mary’",
    "text": "The March 18 episode of \"New Heights\" with Jason Kelce and Travis Kelce featured Ryan Gosling, who promoted the film adaptation of Andy Weir's \"Project Hail Mary\" novel. \"It was an incredible book before it was a film,\" Gosling said. \"Andy Weir wrote this book that has become considered one of the best science fiction books of all time. Many people say it's one of the best books they've ever read. So, we were already hitting the ground running. I've never been a part of a film where I kind of knew people were gonna like it because this book had already been stress tested.\" The box office numbers since the March 20 theatrical release of Project Hail Mary would indicate that people really like it.According to The Hollywood Reporter, the Gosling vehicle notched a $80.6 million domestic launch, which was good enough for \"the best showing of the year.\" As of Sunday, Project Hail Mary is the top-grossing film of 2026.NEW YORK, NEW YORK - MARCH 18: Ryan Gosling attends \"Project Hail Mary\" New York premiere at Lincoln Center on March 18, 2026 in New York City. (Photo...THR also relayed, \"Hail Mary follows Christopher Nolan’s Oppenheimer as only the second non-sequel or non-franchise installment of the past decade to open to $80 million or more domestically. Gosling’s top-grossing film of all time, of course, is Barbie, but Hail Mary is his biggest domestic opening featuring the actor in a leading role, not adjusted for inflation. It is also a domestic best for [Phil] Lord and [Christopher] Miller.\"Lord and Miller directed the movie that stars Gosling as Ryland Grace, a science teacher who wakes up with amnesia aboard a spaceship. He's alone, except for an alien-like creature named Rocky (James Ortiz). Ryland must save the Earth from \"a mysterious substance killing Earth's sun,\" per IMDb.Where to Stream Project Hail MaryAs evidenced by the box-office haul, millions of people have already seen Project Hail Mary. But a 96% Popcornmeter on Rotten Tomatoes suggests they'd want to watch it again. If you haven't been able to make it to the theatre, you may have to wait a little while before Project Hail Mary hits streaming. Project Hail Mary is an Amazon MGM Studios production, so it should eventually find a home on Amazon Prime Video. Apple TV also has a landing page and a \"Coming Soon\" tag for Project Hail Mary if you search for it in the Apple TV app. Last April, The New York Times' Nicole Sperling reported on Amazon's theatre-to-streaming release strategy. She noted, \"Now with 14 movies a year, Amazon’s lineup will rival those from the big studios in both size and scope, and most will spend 45 days in theaters before hitting pay-per-view and then Prime.\"That does not definitively mean that Project Hail Mary will hit Prime by early May, but you can tentatively circle late spring or summer for your at-home viewing.",
